As a C Driver, you are responsible for driving the truck and delivering a wide range of food and non-food products to customers such as restaurants, cafés, sports clubs, and company canteens. Together with your driver’s assistant, you handle loading and unloading and ensure deliveries are completed safely and efficiently.

This is an active role where you are frequently on the move and work in all weather conditions. You will primarily work from Monday to Friday, with regular shifts on Saturdays. Your start time is fixed, but flexibility is required regarding your finishing time.

At the start of the day, you review the route together, load the truck, and begin your deliveries. You also handle basic administrative tasks and provide friendly, customer-focused service. After completing your route, you return to the depot and check in for any additional assignments.

If you perform well, you will have the opportunity to obtain your CE license and grow within the company.

- Valid Category C driving licence and Code 95;
- In possession of a digital driver card;
- Own transport (car/moped/scooter/motorcycle);
- Experience as a driver;
- Living in the vicinity of Berkel en Rodenrijs;
- Presentable appearance;
- Available full-time and flexible;
- Good command of the English language, both spoken and written;

From the job description, you may have already noticed that this is a physically demanding role in which you do more than just drive the vehicle. It is therefore important that this suits you. If so, we encourage you to apply. Who knows, you might soon start working for our client.

Position: Dental Hygienist
Location: Steenwijk – The Netherlands

Information about the employer:
Steenwijkerdiep is a dental practice in Steenwijk. Our modern group practice offers a broad scope of dental care, delivered by a multidisciplinary team of dentists, dental hygienists, and dental assistants. Using advanced equipment and high-quality materials, we strive to provide the highest standard of care.

Information about the position:
As our Dental Hygienist, you play a key role in helping patients achieve and maintain excellent oral health. You will independently perform a wide range of preventive and periodontal treatments, including scaling and polishing, fluoride applications, sealants, dental X-rays, and dental impressions. Working closely with dentists and dental assistants, you will deliver high-quality patient care while educating and motivating patients to adopt healthy oral hygiene habits. This is a hands-on role where your expertise, communication skills, and patient-centered approach make a real difference every day.

Requirements:
- A diploma in Oral Health Care / Dental Hygiene;
- Minimum B1 level English and willing to learn the Dutch language;
- A completed Hepatitis B titer test;
- A valid X-ray certificate;

What we offer:
- A salary (with Dutch registration) between €3400 and €5000 gross per month, depending on qualifications, experience and competencies;
- Annual contract (32 - 40 hours p/w) with intention for a permanent contract;
- Travel allowance;
- Excellent secondary conditions;
- Paid vacation days plus 8% holiday allowance;
- Staff discounts
- Team activities and a pleasant, professional working environment;
- Support in finding accommodation in The Netherlands;

Would you like to work in a modern dental practice where prevention, periodontal care, and teamwork are central?

For more information about the process of recognition of your foreign diploma and the possibilities to work during that period, please send an email to: melvin.zalmijn@uwv.nl

Certified nursing assistant (CNA)

Organisation
The care in the Netherlands is innovative and continuously evolving, known internationally for its efficiency, quality and personal attention for both patient and care professional. Due to the open culture, international careers and nurses are welcome in the Netherlands for an exciting career.

Zorg groep Beek supports you as a care professional in finding long-term employment with the most renowned nursing and care organizations in the Netherlands. Zorg groep Beek offers you:
Professional guidance throughout the recruitment process
- Personal assessment
- Dutch language schooling, A2 level
- Practical support: BSN (citizen service number), accommodation, transport
- Accreditation of diplomas and registration with the right registers
A workplace with a suitable care institution, which immediately becomes your employer and with which you sign a direct employment contract.
Guidance with your employer for 3 years, with your own community, training, coaching and practical matters.
HiNurse: Follow your passion abroad.

We are looking for enthusiastic Care assistants EQF 3 for the provision of care in the care departments of nursing and care homes in the province of Limburg, Netherlands.

Care assistant EQF 3
Job description
The activities with the patients are varied and comprise, among other things:
- caring for, nursing and guiding the clients in accordance with the life care plans;
- (under supervision) drawing up or adjusting life care plans in accordance with the needs of the client;
- coordinating the provision of care and services within a care department;
- monitoring and promoting the quality and quantity of care provided;
- liaising with and collaborating with the care coordinator;
- issuing and administering medicines.
Requirements
You must have a passion for the provision of top quality care, paying sincere attention to the client!
Besides this, as a candidate we seek from you:
- strong communication and social skills;
- care assistant diploma - EQF 3;
- English level B1;
- a strong sense of responsibility and empathy;
- demonstrating initiative and creativity in proposing solutions;
- working in accordance with the ruling norms and quality standards.
What we offer
- employment contract with a permanent contract;
- excellent employment conditions and salary in accordance with the collective labour agreement for the care sector (CAO VVT);
- friendly colleagues;
- Professional care organisation committed to a pleasant working atmosphere and job satisfaction;
- Possibilities for schooling and for growth and development.
